    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0365" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v02/pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.51G9/22</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-17">December 17, 1940</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>During my conversation with the Foreign Minister today I spoke emphatically on
                    the matter of shipment of American-owned goods from Indochina, repeating my
                    representations of November 15 and 30, and in a signed note (no. 1714, December
                    17, 1940<anchor n="15" xml:id="d213-f1"/>) decried the continued and unwarranted
                    interference.</p>
                <closer><signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oseph</hi>] C. G[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">rew</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
